@@ -457,3 +457,7 @@
 Cancellation without a definitive task result remains `unknown`, and terminal
 callback duplicates do not change the receipt. Existing peer delegation receipts
 and transport/task outcome separation remain unchanged.
+
+## Structured messages during a running turn
+
+`HarnessAgent.steer_message` and `HarnessAgentManager.steer_message` accept an optional `message=HumanMessage(...)`. The host validates attachment ownership and versions before admission. Public `text` remains separate from model content. Checkpoints retain message content and metadata; user events contain public text and attachment metadata only. `queue_if_busy=True` buffers up to ten messages in arrival order at the next safe boundary. The default preserves explicit busy rejection. Completed tool results are retained.
